Fever Line (feverline)

Inspired by Pandemic.

Game design, rules text, cards, role portraits, code and art: Luis Montes. The rules are restated in our own words; the
fevers and roles are our own. The maps are real places: games/feverline/tools/gen-maps.mjs picks each map's cities
and links them by its own rules (population, spacing, a Delaunay triangulation cut to its Gabriel edges, k-means
regions), and games/feverline/tools/make-textures.mjs draws the boards, the deck backs, the table and the 2D art.
The sounds are synthesised in code.

Map data:
- City names, places and populations: GeoNames (geonames.org), licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Extract in games/feverline/data/places.tsv (towns and cities only,
  short names kept as given, New York City and Ho Chi Minh City shortened).
- Coastlines: Natural Earth (naturalearthdata.com), public domain.

Built with cartwheel-engine and three.c (MIT). The font is the engine's built-in sans (see the engine's NOTICE).
